// Workspace settings for THIS folder only (codespace-starter). Unlike the
// settings in .devcontainer/devcontainer.json, which apply to every folder
// in the Codespace — including the student's own repo — these apply only
// while codespace-starter is the open folder.
//
// Hide everything from the Explorer so the starting view is as simple as
// possible (David, 2026-10-09): students start from the terminal and the
// READY banner, and connect-repo opens their own repo, where nothing is
// hidden.
//   - .devcontainer: the launcher itself. Tutorials that look inside it use
//     the terminal (`ls .devcontainer`, `code .devcontainer/devcontainer.json`),
//     which the Explorer setting does not affect.
//   - .github: the launcher-tests CI workflow.
//   - .vscode: this file.
// (.devcontainer/tests was listed separately before .devcontainer itself
// was hidden; it stays listed so hiding survives if .devcontainer is ever
// shown again.)
// Hidden, not deleted: CI still runs on every launcher change, and the
// folders still show on GitHub and in `ls -a`. If the setting were moved to
// devcontainer.json it would hide .github in students' own repos too.
{
  "files.exclude": {
    ".devcontainer": true,
    ".github": true,
    ".devcontainer/tests": true,
    ".vscode": true
  }
}
